# Empty and reversed integer ranges

Verifies `for` loops over `10..10` and `10..5` execute zero iterations:
a reversed range never iterates downward, it simply produces no values.
Both cases run through the complete CLI pipeline.

>>> source
for (i in 10..10) {
    print(i)
}

for (i in 10..5) {
    print(i)
}

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
